      "message": "Can\u0027t call into the app code with this internal lock held.  There generally shouldn\u0027t be a need for locking on this, since all access is serialized through the looper.  I would guess that the only time this would be a problem is the situation where you are using WallpaperService in a separate looper, which we used to do for when it was running in the system process...  but now that it is in the system UI process, I think we no longer do that, and in fact does the API to do this even exist any more?",
